Loom: an iu4 WMMA whose accumulator is a splat of the i32 bits of 1/(2 pi) selects a form with that inline source in
SRC2 (`.acc_inv_2pi`, beside `.acc_zero`), x - c with an inline f32 constant c selects v_subrev_f32 with c in src0,
and VOPD pairs such a subrev (new BINARY_SRC0_INLINE component form: the inline source needs no register bank). Yah
seeds the iu4 GEMM accumulators with those bits: read as f32 the result is 1/(2 pi) + c * 2^-26 exactly, so one
paired subtract replaces the int-to-float conversion (activation scales stored times 2^26). Bit-identical results;
fold VALU -19% per phase, pp2048 GEMM cycles unchanged (the shorter loop waits on its next-phase loads).
